      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="615" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding a bifunctional enzyme expressing both uridine activity (UK) and uracil phosphoribosyltransferase activity (UPRT) has been identified in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The uridine kinase activity was found in the N-terminal region whereas the uracil phosphoribosyltransferase activity was located in the C-terminal region. The molecular function of UK, i.e. catalyzing the formation of uridine 5&apos;-monophosphate (UMP) from uridine and adenine 5&apos;-triphosphate (ATP) and UPRT, i.e. catalyzing the formation of UMP from uracil and phosphoribosyl-alpha-1-pyrophosphate (PRPP), respectively was confirmed in mutants and double mutants of &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. These mutants were unable to express UK and/or UPRT activities and therefore unable to use either the uracil compound equivalent 5-fluorouracil (5-FU) or the uridine compound equivalent 5-fluorouridine (5-FD). Wildtype bacteria treated with this compounds show severely retarded growth and this phentotype could be rescued from the unimpaired mutants by transgenic expressing the corresponding AtUT/UPRT1 gene from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thalaiana&lt;/i&gt;. The same results were obtained by expression of the single UT or UPRT domains from AtUT/UPTR1 in those mutants. In addition, Arabidopsis wildtype plants also show a retardation growth phenotype and a severe loss of chlorophyll after treatment with 5-FU and 5-FD whereas an Arabidopsis T-DNA insertion mutant defective in the corresponding gene (At5g40870, AtUT/UPRT1) was not impaired at all |CITS: [17143579]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G40870-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G40870.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9FKS0" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAM10488" />
