    <DataNode elementId="AT5G63310-MONOMER" textLabel="Nucleoside pyrophosphate kinase II, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64903" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="695" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding nucleoside diphosphate kinase 2 (AtNDK-2) was identified from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and recombinant expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The molecular function of catalyzing the exchange transfer of a &amp;gamma;-phosphoryl group from a nucleoside triphosphate to a nucleoside diphosphate was confirmed with purified recombinant protein and the structure and mode of action demonstrated in the crystallized protein |CITS: [15465053]|. AtNDK-2 has been shown to be involved in the phytochrome mediated growth and developmental processes by interacting with the C-terminal domain of phytochrome A (PhyA) |CITS: [15561724]|. In addition AtNDK-2 takes part in cellular redox regulation by interacting with activated mitogen-activated protein kinases (MAPKs) conferring tolerance to environmental stresses such as reactive oxygen species (ROS) accumulation |CITS: [12506203]|. Furthermore, AtNDK-2 has been reported to be involved in auxin-regulated processes, particularly through the mediation of polar auxin transport |CITS: [15927941]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G63310-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G63310.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64903" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAC15253" />
